        "id": "ch4_1-2",
        "text": "If I were to do that in a more Java-like style, I would write this:\nNew-Variable -Name MyVariable\nSet-Variable -Name MyVariable -Value 'some stuff'\nWhich creates a variable, gives it a name, and then we put a value in it. In practice, this is very rare.\nMost people, in most situations, create variables on the fly.\nIf you read those lines of code closely, you will see that the first example contains $MyVariable ,\nand in the second one, it\u2019s MyVariable , without the $ sign. Let\u2019s talk about why.\nEsta secci\u00f3n contiene las siguientes subsecciones\n\u2022 Variables are not their contents\n\u2022 Naming variables\n\u2022 The three common types of PowerShell variable\nSi deseas explorar cualquiera de estas subsecciones, puedes pregunt\u00e1rmelo directamente.",
